 "code": "await rlm.harness.create_memory(title='ARC line-grid extraction task fe7ed708', content='Task-fe7ed708 is a repeating grid puzzle: input is a large regular lattice of uniform-background rectangular cells, separated by line-color grid. At some intersections along separator lines, anomalous colors occur. Output is a much smaller matrix encoding anomalous intersection values in a selected rectangular window, with the regular interior/background cell color used for positions without anomaly. Demos establish outputs: demo1 input 30x28 with background2 and boundaries every 8 rows/5 cols -> 3x4 output [[9,2,2,3],[9,2,2,2],[9,2,2,2]]. demo2 bg9 output 3x4 [[6,9,9,7],[9,6,9,9],[9,9,9,5]]. demo3 bg0 output 2x6 [[5,0,0,2,0,1],[5,5,0,0,0,1]]. demo4 bg5 output 6x2 [[5,1],[5,5],[5,2],[2,5],[5,5],[5,3]]. demo5 bg8 output 5x4 [[9,8,8,8],[8,8,8,9],[6,8,9,8],[8,8,8,8],[8,6,8,9]]. demo6 output 1x1 [[0]]. demo7 bg3 output 5x3 [[3,1,3],[1,3,3],[3,3,4],[6,3,3],[6,3,7]]. Deduced likely extraction translates marked intersection pattern to downsampled grid, using base interior color for unmarked locations; dimensions vary according to selected marked region. For test input rows/columns separator crossings were many; 8 failed guesses, no known correct. Guesses explored sampling boundaries and selecting crop; none validated. Main actionable insight: do not simply output all crossing markers or assume fixed matrix size. Analyze precisely which subset of crossings maps to output; output background equals interior fill color (not separator line color).",
